WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
(group cheering)

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:02.940
- [Narrator] Residents of Kherson

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.900
cheered Ukrainian soldiers,
tore down Russian posters,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.540
and raised Ukrainian flags.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.580
These verified videos posted online

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.470
by Ukrainian journalists and officials

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.000
show celebrations in Kherson

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.893
after Russia retreated from the city.

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:19.320
Just a few weeks earlier,

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.970
Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.640
claimed and celebrated
the annexation of Kherson,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.250
the only regional capital
that Moscow had captured

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.650
since invading Ukraine in February.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.720
The withdrawal from the
strategic southern city

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.300
is a major symbolic
defeat for the Kremlin.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.000
We look back at the key
moments in how Russia captured

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.503
and then lost Kherson.

00:00:38.658 --> 00:00:40.320
(engines rumbling)

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.840
This is the day when Russian
tanks rolled into Kherson,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.850
the first major Ukrainian city to fall

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.516
during the first few weeks of the war.

00:00:46.516 --> 00:00:49.933
(group shouting angrily)

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.500
- [Narrator] But soon
after the occupation,

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.320
local residents came out
in droves to protest.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.964
Demonstrations lasted for weeks,

00:00:56.964 --> 00:00:58.050
(gunfire rattling)

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.453
and in some instances, gunshots rang out.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.170
In the following months,
the Kremlin laid out plans

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.780
to turn Kherson into a Russian city.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:09.390
The Russian ruble became an
officially accepted currency,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.310
and Russian citizenship was fast-tracked

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.459
for willing residents.

00:01:12.459 --> 00:01:14.820
(man speaking foreign language)

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.860
- [Narrator] By June, Russian
state media showed footage

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.300
of the first Kherson residents

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.930
receiving their new documents,

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.090
(rocket whooshing)

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.220
but around this time,
Washington started shipping

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.500
the first units of HIMARS to Ukraine.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.240
These are long-range rocket launchers

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.863
and a game-changer in the war.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.460
This enabled Ukrainian troops
to begin targeting bridges

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.470
over the Dnipro River, which links Kherson

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.723
to other Russian-occupied territories.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.960
As Ukrainian forces started retaking parts

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:43.170
of southern Ukraine, Moscow
held sham referendums in Kherson

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.750
and three other regions
asking remaining residents

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:47.500
whether they wanted to join Russia.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.430
A few days later, Putin signed treaties

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.470
to annex Kherson and
the other territories,

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.020
and celebrations were held in Moscow.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.400
The annexation wasn't recognized

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.370
by any foreign government
apart from North Korea.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.110
Only a few weeks after the annexation,

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:03.720
Russia began mass transfer
of residents from Kherson,

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.300
saying up to 70,000
people would be evacuated

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.921
as Ukrainian forces
advanced toward the city

00:02:08.921 --> 00:02:13.004
(Alla speaking foreign language)

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.320
- [Narrator] Ukrainian
soldiers also used artillery

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.230
to cut off thousands of Russian
troops in and around Kherson

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.569
by targeting bridges in the area.

00:02:21.569 --> 00:02:25.819
(Sergei speaking foreign language)

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.620
- [Narrator] After Moscow said

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.910
it had completed its withdrawal,

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:32.370
Ukraine confirmed that its
troops had entered the city,

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.870
marking a turning point in the war

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.098
and a morale boost for Ukrainians

00:02:36.098 --> 00:02:40.598
(Volodymyr speaking foreign language)

00:02:43.779 --> 00:02:44.612
- [Narrator] While the retreat

00:02:44.612 --> 00:02:45.960
is a political blow for Putin,

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.780
Russia still controls
parts of the Kherson region

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.300
and Moscow says it will
now hold stronger positions

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.100
to the east of Kherson
where it'll be easier

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.845
to resupply its troops
as the war grinds on.

00:02:55.845 --> 00:02:58.962
(dramatic piano music)

